Feature: EN 1991 check outcome of committed documents
  A committed document (mutation snapshots and the hand-built `actions-all-*` fixtures) is evaluated by the production report and by the document oracle `../../🔮️oracles/🚦️check-outcome/🐍️.py` (required over assumed: imposed, concentrated, partitions, self-weight, snow, wind, fire gas temperature, net heat flux, fire load, thermal, construction, impact; third-party: scipy.stats, scipy.integrate, scipy.constants).
  Each row names one check id, its status (pass at a utilisation of at most 1, fail above 1) and its utilisation; rows were picked away from the near-limit band so the status is unambiguous.

